Package: ellstat
Type: Package
Title: Elliptic Moments for Circular Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("M. Theodor", "Loots", email = "theo.loots@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7722-3913"))
Description: Elliptic moments generalise trigonometric moments by replacing the
    circular functions with the Jacobi elliptic functions of a given modulus, so
    that modulus zero recovers the trigonometric system exactly. Every member of
    the family exists unconditionally and characterises the distribution, the
    sample moments are unbiased at every sample size with exactly known variance
    and joint covariance, and exact Monte Carlo tests and confidence intervals
    follow by direct simulation of the null and by test inversion over a nuisance
    set. The efficiency of a moment estimator relative to maximum likelihood is
    the squared correlation between the statistic and the score, which
    characterises the optimal modulus. Routines are provided for the basis, the
    transfer to trigonometric moments, the elliptic von Mises family, the
    arc-length family on an ellipse and the projected normal and Cauchy laws, on
    a C back end shared with a Python front.
